  "notes": "Topline specialist supplying the melodic and lyric architecture for the current chart-pop board. She is a writer rather than a programmer, and the research is honest about that — but it still yields a drum grammar, because the melodies are written against one: \"her toplines are written against a syncopated 16th groove with gaps on downbeats — the melodies are built to land in the holes, which is why the records she writes on tend to have sparse, hole-punched drum patterns.\" That is authored as the three deltas the sentence actually contains: `kick.beatSkipProb` 0.36 (the holes on downbeats), `kick.syncopation` 0.6 with a 16th-heavy `offbeat8thShare` (the syncopated 16th groove), and a `percs` bed at 16th density with the kick density itself held low (sparse). The bass claim is equally usable: \"her toplines characteristically sit above a loud syncopated bass line rather than a sustained pad\", so the bassline is `independent_riff` at 0.32 with a high `anticipationProb`, and no `bass808` block is authored because none is described. Harmony is \"minor-mode verses with a bright chorus lift, and major-key disco/funk vamps on the recent catalogue\", with her documented instinct \"toward darker, more serious songs\" as the reason minor carries the higher weight even under an up-tempo groove. The melody block is the entry itself: her 1990s singer-songwriter influence set \"shows as conversational, punchline-shaped short phrases with a narrow interval span and a spoken aside as the tag\", which is a small `motifPitchCount`, a narrow register, a 1—2 bar phrase and `endVariation`; \"she also sings background vocals on the records she writes, so the harmony stacks are close unison\" is the low counter density. The arrangement is her stated signature: the title hook in the first two bars of the chorus, a post-chorus repeating a fragment, a spoken outro. ⚠ `confidence` is medium against a medium-high rating because the research says \"the rhythmic-placement claim is inferred from those records\": every drum probability, the humanize pair and `bpm.mode` 125 (the midpoint of the stated 100—150 band) are INFERRED.",
